{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 3, :comments ["<b>And the hair in the lesion has turned white.</b> A sign that the flesh has weakened, that the lesion kills the flesh; even old men, similarly, when they weaken their hair turns white. But if the hair turned white before the lesion came, this is not a sign of impurity, since it did not turn white because of the lesion. And so our Rabbis said: if the baheret precedes the white hair — impure; if not — pure." "<b>And he declares him impure.</b> By speech."], :book :leviticus, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 13, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:11:41.907311922Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}